# Specification - Phase 2: UI Improvements & UX Polish

## Requirements

Implement core Taskwarrior WebUI UX improvements:

1. **#51 Pre-fill Project and Assignee on New Task**:
   - When the user is viewing a filtered project in the UI and clicks to add a new task, the "Project" field in the task creation dialog must be pre-filled with the active project (ignoring `(All Projects)` and `(No Project)`).
   - When an assignee filter is active (ignoring `(All Assignees)` and `(Unassigned)`), pre-fill the "Assignee" field in the new task modal with the filtered assignee.
   - Fallback: If no specific assignee filter is active, pre-fill Assignee from the default `assigneeName` configured in user Settings (`store.state.settings.assigneeName`), if present.

2. **#77 Bulk Add (Brain Dump Mode)**:
   - Streamline rapid successive task entry inside the "Add Task" modal.
   - Support keyboard shortcut `Ctrl+Enter` (or `Cmd+Enter` on macOS) to save the current task immediately and keep the modal open with focus returned to the Description field for the next entry.
   - In Bulk Add mode, retain the currently selected `Project` and `Assignee` across successive entries, while resetting `Description`, `customCommand`, `annotations`, `depends`, and dates.
   - Standard `Enter` (or clicking "Save") saves the task and closes the dialog.

3. **#47 Date & Time Pickers for Task Dates**:
   - Integrate Vuetify date & time picker popups / menus (`v-date-picker` / `v-time-picker`) beside date fields (`due`, `until`, `scheduled`, `wait`) triggered by calendar/clock append icons.
   - Preserve direct text editing so users can still type relative Taskwarrior date strings (e.g. `tomorrow`, `eod`, `friday`, `2d`).

4. **#74 & #22 Remember Sorting Order & Frontend Preferences**:
   - Persist user frontend table options across page reloads using `localStorage`.
   - Store table sorting options (sort column `sortBy`, sort descending `sortDesc`, and rows per page `itemsPerPage`).
   - Restore table options seamlessly on page load without layout shift or UI flickering.

## Clarifications & Decisions
- **Date/Time Picker Integration (#47)**: Keep text fields for direct input, and add an icon button on each date input to open a `v-menu` with date/time pickers that formats the selected date into the field.
- **Bulk Add State Retention (#77)**: On `Ctrl+Enter`, save the task, clear Description and annotations, but keep Project and Assignee populated for fast entry under the same context.
- **Pre-fill Fallback (#51)**: Active filter takes precedence. If no filter is active, Assignee falls back to `settings.assigneeName`.

## User Stories
- As a user entering tasks under a specific project and assignee, I want those fields automatically pre-filled so I don't have to retype them repeatedly.
- As a user doing a brain dump of multiple tasks, I want to press `Ctrl+Enter` to rapidly submit task after task without having to reopen the dialog each time.
- As a user scheduling deadlines, I want visual date/time pickers to select dates accurately while still having the freedom to type relative date shortcuts.
- As a user who customized column sorting and page sizes, I want those preferences remembered across browser sessions.
